  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BARMM Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the BARMM RESILIENCE activity is to enhance the local capacity of the BARMM Ministry of Health and the BARMM provinces and cities to pursue key and cross-cutting reforms in health systems.  The activity will focus on strengthening health governance, financing, supply chain and logistics, human resources for health, and health information to provide a more conducive setting to implement Tuberculosis (TB), Family Planning and Adolescent Reproductive Health (FP/ARH), and Global Health Security (GHS) programs. To promote resilience, the activity will fortify local health systems, as well as local ownership and capacity in pandemic preparedness and response, while bolstering positive social norms and healthy behaviors, and improving the quality of primary health care services. The activity will align with the Universal Health Care law&#x2019;s implementing rules and regulation for the BARMM region issued by the BARMM government.</narrative>
  </description>
